## Persona 4 Revival at a glance

Persona 4 Revival is ATLUS's full remake of Persona 4 Golden, published by SEGA. The visuals, interface, battles and story events have all been rebuilt. SEGA's official site calls it a good starting point for newcomers to the series that should still feel fresh to fans of the original.

The release day depends on where you look. The English Steam listing shows **17 February 2027**, and SEGA's official site says **18 February 2027**. A one-day gap like this usually comes from time zones. Check your own store region for the exact day and time it unlocks. Both dates were checked on 26 November 2026.

## What we know so far

- **Developer:** ATLUS. **Publisher:** SEGA.
- **Release date:** 17 February 2027 on English Steam, 18 February 2027 on SEGA's site.
- **Platforms:** SEGA's site lists Xbox Series X|S, Game Pass, the Microsoft Store on PC, PlayStation 5, Steam and Nintendo Switch 2.
- **Price on Steam (US):** $69.99 for the standard edition.
- **Editions:** Digital Standard, Digital Deluxe and Digital Premium. Deluxe adds a Velvet outfit set and sets of Personas from Persona 3 Reload and Persona 5 Royal. Premium also adds costume sets and music packs from both games. SEGA's site also offers a physical version.
- **Pre-order bonus:** an Extra BGM Set with music tracks from Persona 3 Reload and Persona 5 Royal. Steam says it is available for pre-orders made by 17 February 2027, 23:59 ET.
- **Trailers:** Steam shows a Teaser Trailer, a Story Trailer and a Pre-Order Trailer.

## The story

The game is set in Inaba, a quiet country town in Japan. A rumour among local teenagers says that if you stare at a switched-off TV at midnight on a rainy night, the "Midnight Channel" shows you your destined partner. Then people start disappearing and are later found dead in strange circumstances.

You and your friends form an investigation team. You travel between the real world and a fog-filled world inside the TV, where Shadows roam. In this game, Shadows are the hidden sides of people's personalities that they refuse to accept. When a character faces their Shadow and accepts it, it awakens as a Persona, which they then use to fight.

## How it plays

The official descriptions confirm the core of the original game:

- **Turn-based battles.** You exploit enemy weaknesses, use "All-Out Attacks", and gain or fuse new Personas.
- **School life.** You balance sports, part-time jobs, school and friendships through the year. SEGA's site also mentions studying, club activities, karaoke and romance.
- **Relationships.** Building bonds with characters affects your journey. The publisher says your choices lead to different experiences and endings.
- **Updated presentation.** Anime-style and 3D cutscenes have been redone, with what the publisher calls quality-of-life improvements.

## What's still unconfirmed

- **Exactly what changed from Persona 4 Golden:** SEGA says visuals, UI, battles and events were reimagined, but has not published a full list of added, removed or changed content.
- **PC requirements:** Steam lists the operating system as "TBD" and gives no hardware details.
- **Performance on each platform:** we haven't played Persona 4 Revival on any system.
- **Whether the date will hold:** these are the dates shown on 26 November 2026. Release dates can still change.

